# TASK-260728-yx2fca results

## Outcome

Revised the candidate-neutral SSH contract from full-fidelity M0 to the human-approved M0 viability scope. The code registry classifies 16 requirements as M0-viability-mandatory and exactly four semantics as M3-deferred under TASK-260728-3cveay. libssh2 remains primary; ReluxNIOSSH remains comparative evidence with no new fork work.

The neutral seam now requires explicit reported, notReported, or unsupported values for consumer-driven receive-credit/cap policy and snapshots, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit/coreDumped metadata, KEX generation, window/server-rekey/keepalive deep metrics, and keepalive RTT. Mandatory host-before-auth, approved public-key authentication, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client and server rekey handling, bounded buffers/backpressure, deterministic cancellation/lifecycle, Keychain-only references, keepalive transmission, available observability, and privacy-safe errors remain ordinary requirements.

## Contract and consumers

Canonical contract: .spec/ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md. SHA-256 0806310f5caee9244cfc77d5ae9f45aa87a43684290402638f57b2aa53e39114. The original TASK-260715-2ny6z4 outcome and preconditions on TASK-260715-1ozsb6, TASK-260715-2d3g5e, TASK-260715-1u2vpc, and TASK-260728-3cveay are byte-identical to the canonical revision. All three named consumer ACs explicitly reference the M0-viability tier and the four M3 states.

Retained evidence remains attached: TASK-260715-1ozsb6_libssh2-rekey-blocker.md, TASK-260715-1ozsb6_server-rekey-keepalive-blocker.md, TASK-260715-1ozsb6_third-public-api-blocker.md, TASK-260715-1af33i_adapter-api-blocker.md, TASK-260715-1af33i_window-gap-test-01.log, and TASK-260715-28ok1k_ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md.

## Validation

- Initial required status command: exit 1 because estimate was required; set Fibonacci estimate 5, then status transition exit 0.
- Baseline focused SSH suite: exit 0, 12 tests.
- First strict format gate: exit 1; formatted the two reported expressions. Final strict recursive Swift format: exit 0.
- First post-policy-split compile: exit 1 for one missing test-helper return; fixed.
- Final focused SSH suite: exit 0, 13 tests.
- git diff --check: exit 0.
- check-core-boundaries.sh: exit 0.
- make validate-core: exit 0; native/libssh2 verification passed, 336 tests in 29 suites passed, swift build passed.
- task-board validate: command exit 0 and reports PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH for STORY-260715-lkshfz because unfinished hard blocker STORY-260715-l2i2oo suppresses parent promotion while this leaf is development. No dependency was bypassed; anomaly recorded in LOGBOOK.md.

No external blocker remains. Ready for developer-to-review handoff.
